Maintainer: Alireza Khodadadi-Jamayran <alireza.khodadadi.j@gmail.com>
Description: Tools for large-scale single-cell and spatial omics analysis
    with a familiar R interface. The package is designed for multimodal
    projects including scRNA-seq, scATAC-seq, multiome, scVDJ-seq,
    CITE-seq/ADT, spatial transcriptomics, Visium, Xenium, and
    proteomics or mass spectrometry data. It provides methods for data
    import, quality control, filtering, normalization, dimensionality
    reduction, graph construction, clustering, marker detection,
    differential expression, batch correction, cell type annotation,
    pseudotime analysis, and multimodal integration. iCellR2 is designed
    around an R frontend, a C++ core, on-disk sparse storage,
    HDF5-backed data handling, chunked operations, multithreading,
    optional Python/GPU backends, and sketch/projection workflows for
    scalable analysis of very large datasets.
Depends: R (>= 3.3.0)
